      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Five patients with McArdle's disease entered a double-blind, placebo-controlled, cross-over study of dantrolene sodium. None of the patients experienced beneficial effect of dantrolene sodium medication. Each patient performed 2 exercise tests. Surface EMG during exercise tests without medication showed a temporary increase in EMG activity during the adaptation phase. Quite unexpectedly however, in view of the negative clinical results, this electrophysiological manifestation of muscle fatigue during the adaptation phase diminished or disappeared in all patients investigated when dantrolene sodium was used."},
